    {
      "title": "Views: The Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Views: The Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a View Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A view is a ==named, stored SELECT==",
                "It holds {red:no data} of its own",
                "Each query on it ==re-runs== the underlying query"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "CREATE VIEW active_users AS",
                "  SELECT id, name FROM users WHERE active = 1;",
                "SELECT * FROM active_users;"
              ],
              "note": "define once, query like a table"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Outer query",
                    "sub": "uses the view",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Inlining",
                    "sub": "optimizer merges",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Base tables",
                    "sub": "one plan",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Updatable Views",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE ==pass through== to the base table",
                "Merged into the outer query, so a view is {orange:not a cache}"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "View query has",
                "Updatable?"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Single base table, plain columns",
                  "{green:Yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "DISTINCT, GROUP BY, aggregates",
                  "{red:No}"
                ],
                [
                  "UNION or window functions",
                  "{red:No}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Stacked views",
              "text": "Views on views hide cost and make plans unreadable. `CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW` can ==add== columns, not drop or reorder them."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Updatable Views and Security via Views",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Updatable Views and Security via Views",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. WITH CHECK OPTION",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==WITH CHECK OPTION== rejects INSERT or UPDATE through the view that would give a row the view **cannot show**"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "CREATE VIEW eu_orders AS",
                "  SELECT * FROM orders",
                "  WHERE region='EU' WITH CHECK OPTION;",
                "",
                "INSERT INTO eu_orders (region)",
                "  VALUES ('US');  -- rejected"
              ],
              "note": "region='US' fails the view's WHERE"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Security via Views",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{green:GRANT SELECT} on the view, {red:REVOKE} on the base table",
                "View exposes only chosen ==columns== and ==rows==",
                "Column hiding: `emp_public` leaves out `salary`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "CREATE VIEW emp_public AS",
                "  SELECT id, name, dept FROM employees;",
                "REVOKE ALL ON employees FROM analyst;",
                "GRANT SELECT ON emp_public TO analyst;"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. PostgreSQL Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Default",
                "`security_invoker = true`"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Runs with",
                  "view **owner's** privileges",
                  "**caller's** privileges"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Leaky function in the view's WHERE can expose hidden rows",
                "Fix: create the view with ==security_barrier=="
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Materialized Views and Refresh",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Materialized Views and Refresh",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What it stores",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Stores the query result ==physically on disk==",
                "{green:Reads are fast}: no recompute per query",
                "{red:Data can be stale} until refreshed",
                "Can be ==indexed== like a table"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "CREATE MATERIALIZED VIEW daily_sales AS",
                "SELECT day, SUM(amt) total",
                "FROM sales GROUP BY day;"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Refresh",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`REFRESH MATERIALIZED VIEW` (PostgreSQL) ==recomputes everything== and **locks reads**",
                "Add `CONCURRENTLY` to avoid the read lock",
                "`CONCURRENTLY` needs a ==UNIQUE index== on the view",
                "Oracle: **fast (incremental) refresh** via materialized view logs"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "CREATE UNIQUE INDEX ON daily_sales (day);",
                "REFRESH MATERIALIZED VIEW daily_sales;",
                "REFRESH MATERIALIZED VIEW CONCURRENTLY daily_sales;"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. View vs materialized view",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "View",
                "Materialized view"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Data",
                  "stored query only",
                  "stored result"
                ],
                [
                  "Freshness",
                  "{green:always fresh}",
                  "{red:stale} until refreshed"
                ],
                [
                  "Computed",
                  "per query",
                  "at refresh"
                ],
                [
                  "Indexable",
                  "no",
                  "yes"
                ],
                [
                  "Best for",
                  "simple, live reads",
                  "heavy aggregates"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Materialized view = ==stored result + REFRESH==. Fast reads cost freshness; use `CONCURRENTLY` plus a unique index to refresh without blocking readers."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Stored Procedures and Functions",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Stored Procedures and Functions",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Procedure vs Function",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Stored procedure==: named, precompiled SQL block kept in the DB",
                "Run standalone: `CALL archive_orders(30);`",
                "Parameters: `IN`, `OUT`, `INOUT`",
                "Can control transactions: `COMMIT` / `ROLLBACK`",
                "==Function==: returns a value or table, used inside `SELECT`",
                "Example: `SELECT tax(amount) FROM orders;`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Function",
                "Procedure"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Called",
                  "Inside an expression",
                  "Standalone with `CALL`"
                ],
                [
                  "Returns",
                  "Value or table",
                  "Nothing required; `OUT` params"
                ],
                [
                  "Transactions",
                  "Usually {red:cannot commit}",
                  "{green:May COMMIT / ROLLBACK}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Example (PostgreSQL)",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "CREATE FUNCTION tax(a numeric)",
                "RETURNS numeric AS $$",
                "  SELECT a*0.18",
                "$$ LANGUAGE sql;"
              ],
              "note": "then: SELECT tax(amount) FROM orders;"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Common Mistake",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Row-by-row loops or cursors inside a procedure are ==slow==",
                "Prefer one set-based `UPDATE` or `INSERT ... SELECT`"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Function = used in `SELECT`, returns a value. Procedure = `CALL`, can commit."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Triggers: BEFORE, AFTER, Row vs Statement",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Triggers: BEFORE, AFTER, Row vs Statement",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a Trigger Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Code that fires ==automatically== on `INSERT`, `UPDATE` or `DELETE` of a table",
                "**Cannot be called directly**, takes no arguments from the caller"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. BEFORE vs AFTER, ROW vs STATEMENT",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Runs",
                "Use for"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "==BEFORE==",
                  "before the write; can change `NEW` or cancel",
                  "validation, defaults"
                ],
                [
                  "==AFTER==",
                  "after the write",
                  "audit logs, cascading changes"
                ],
                [
                  "`FOR EACH ROW`",
                  "once per affected row; has `OLD` and `NEW`",
                  "per-row checks"
                ],
                [
                  "`FOR EACH STATEMENT`",
                  "once per statement, even for 0 rows; no row access",
                  "statement-level logging"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Example",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "CREATE TRIGGER audit_sal",
                "AFTER UPDATE ON emp",
                "FOR EACH ROW",
                "EXECUTE FUNCTION log_change();"
              ],
              "note": "log_change() records OLD.salary and NEW.salary"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Trigger that modifies its **own table** can ==recurse==",
                "They run **invisibly** and ==slow bulk loads==",
                "`INSERT` has no `OLD`; `DELETE` has no `NEW`"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "BEFORE = validate or alter `NEW`. AFTER = audit or propagate."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Database Logic Trade-offs and Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Database Logic Trade-offs and Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. DB or App?",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Keep in the DB",
                "Keep in the app"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Rules",
                  "==Integrity rules==, constraints",
                  "Business workflows"
                ],
                [
                  "Data work",
                  "{green:Audit trails}",
                  "External calls (APIs, email)"
                ],
                [
                  "Volume",
                  "Set operations on many rows",
                  "Logic needing unit tests"
                ],
                [
                  "Why",
                  "No rows over the network",
                  "Version control, easy debug"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Harder to ==test and debug==",
                "Tied to one vendor dialect: `PL/pgSQL`, `PL/SQL`, `T-SQL`",
                "Scales only with the ==database server=="
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Object Cheat Sheet",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Object",
                "Remember"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "View",
                  "Saved query, no data"
                ],
                [
                  "Materialized view",
                  "Stored result + `REFRESH`"
                ],
                [
                  "Procedure",
                  "`CALL`, can ==commit=="
                ],
                [
                  "Function",
                  "Used in `SELECT`, returns a value"
                ],
                [
                  "Trigger",
                  "Auto on event"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Trigger Cheat Sheet",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`BEFORE`: ==validate== or alter `NEW`",
                "`AFTER`: ==audit== or propagate",
                "`ROW`: per row, has `OLD` / `NEW`",
                "`STATEMENT`: once per statement"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "text": "Can you update through a view? Yes if simple: one table, no aggregates. What does `WITH CHECK OPTION` do? It rejects rows the view cannot show. Materialized vs view? Stored and stale vs always fresh. Avoid triggers when they hide logic, recurse or slow bulk loads."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "`eu_orders` is a view on `orders WHERE region='EU'` with WITH CHECK OPTION. What does `INSERT INTO eu_orders (region) VALUES ('US')` do?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "It is rejected: the new row would be invisible through the view.",
                "Without the option, it would insert into `orders` and vanish from the view."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A new sale is inserted into `sales`. You query the materialized view `daily_sales`. Is the sale in the totals?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "No. It stays stale until `REFRESH MATERIALIZED VIEW`.",
                "A plain view would include it, because it re-runs the query each time."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "An UPDATE matches zero rows of `emp`. How often do a FOR EACH ROW trigger and a FOR EACH STATEMENT trigger fire?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Row trigger: 0 times, since there are no rows.",
                "Statement trigger: once, even for zero rows."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
